{
  "_comment": [
    "Pedestal rocks: a broad cap on a stem the blown sand has cut narrow near the ground, as in Egypt's White Desert.",
    "Four shapes to draw from -- a leaning mushroom, a tall slender one, a squat table and a pair grown together --",
    "each a tapered beam flaring up into a cap of overlapping lobes; the cap warped so its outline wanders, the",
    "whole undulated, and the stem run deep into the cap so no size parts them. Posed and sized like the boulders.",
    "About eight across the cap and six tall as written; `largest` 12 makes `colossal` about eighty across.",
    "Mostly one to every few hundred blocks, and where the patches rise, a crowd of them packed twenty apart -- a goblin",
    "valley. Sandstone on sand, red sandstone on red sand, and the level's own stone elsewhere, unless a book names one."
  ],
